      "side": 1,
      "message": "Advisory `warnings` on line 4040 still unconditionally use `output_api.PresubmitPromptWarning(x)`, which will still block AI agents and `CHROME_HEADLESS\u003d1` runs on an interactive `(y/N)` stdin prompt during `git cl upload` whenever `alint` emits a non-blocking `WARNING:` (or emits a warning before a non-zero exit in `run_alint.py`).\n\nThe way Jetski implemented it was defining a shared `warning_factory` and using it for both `json_dict[\"warnings\"]` and `execution_error`:\n\n```python\n        warning_factory \u003d (\n            output_api.PresubmitNotifyResult\n            if (\n                gclient_utils.IsEnvAi(input_api.environ)\n                or input_api.environ.get(\"CHROME_HEADLESS\") \u003d\u003d \"1\"\n            )\n            else output_api.PresubmitPromptWarning\n        )\n        results \u003d [output_api.PresubmitError(x) for x in json_dict[\"errors\"]]\n        results +\u003d [warning_factory(x) for x in json_dict[\"warnings\"]]\n        if \"execution_error\" in json_dict:\n            err \u003d json_dict[\"execution_error\"]\n            msg \u003d f\"AyeAye execution failed (exit code {err[\u0027exit_code\u0027]})\"\n            if err.get(\"output\"):\n                msg +\u003d f\":\\n{err[\u0027output\u0027]}\"\n            msg +\u003d (\n                \"\\nPlease file a bug at http://go/alint-bug if you think this \"\n                \"is an issue.\"\n            )\n            results.append(warning_factory(msg))\n```",
